2025-05-01 01:51:25 - Thread-484 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Below is a quick mapping of the columns that will be useful for building the requested “June‑to‑December 2019” sales report, followed by ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (from very simple to fairly complex).  
Every column name is wrapped in double quotes, all statements are pure SELECTs, and each one is capped with LIMIT 20.

-------------------------------------------------
Relevant columns and how they will be used

• "ORDERS"."order_id"           : join key between ORDERS and ORDER_ITEMS  
• "ORDERS"."created_at"         : order‑creation time‑stamp (µs‑epoch) – used for month filtering & grouping  
• "ORDERS"."user_id"            : can be used to check unique shoppers if needed  
• "ORDER_ITEMS"."order_id"      : link to ORDERS, so we know when the item was ordered  
• "ORDER_ITEMS"."sale_price"    : revenue for that line item  
• "ORDER_ITEMS"."product_id"    : link to PRODUCTS (or to INVENTORY_ITEMS via "inventory_item_id")  
• "PRODUCTS"."id"               : primary key that equals "ORDER_ITEMS"."product_id"  
• "PRODUCTS"."category"         : product category that the final report must break down by  
• "PRODUCTS"."cost"             : unit cost – profit = SUM("sale_price")‑SUM("cost")  
• "ORDER_ITEMS"."created_at"    : item‑level timestamp (µs‑epoch); can be used instead of ORDERS.created_at when convenient  
• "ORDERS"."status"             : we keep every order irrespective of status, but good to confirm the spread

-------------------------------------------------
Exploratory SQLs

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at distinct years in ORDERS to make sure 2019 data exist.
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(year FROM TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000))      AS "order_year"
FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List the months we’ll be analysing (June‑Dec 2019) to verify micro‑second timestamps.
SELECT DISTINCT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000), 'YYYY-MM')     AS "yyyymm"
FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"
WHERE  "created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000  /* 2019‑06‑01 */
                       AND 1577836799000000  /* 2019‑12‑31 23:59:59 */
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Get a feel for the different statuses present in ORDERS (all must be included later).
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"
WHERE  "created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836799000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Look at top 20 product categories that were actually sold in the target timeframe.
SELECT DISTINCT P."category"
FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  OI
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"     P
       ON OI."product_id" = P."id"
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"       O
       ON OI."order_id"  = O."order_id"
WHERE  O."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836799000000
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Sample 20 order‑item lines from July 2019 with their category and basic money fields.
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(O."created_at"/1000000), 'YYYY-MM') AS "month",
       OI."order_id",
       OI."product_id",
       P."category",
       OI."sale_price",
       P."cost"
FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  OI
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"     P  ON OI."product_id" = P."id"
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"       O  ON OI."order_id"  = O."order_id"
WHERE  O."created_at" BETWEEN 1561939200000000 /* 2019‑07‑01 */
                         AND 1564617599000000 /* 2019‑07‑31 23:59:59 */
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Compute revenue & profit by category for one month (August 2019) – sanity check.
SELECT P."category",
       COUNT(*)                                            AS "num_order_items",
       SUM(OI."sale_price")                                AS "revenue",
       SUM(OI."sale_price" - P."cost")                    AS "profit"
FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  OI
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"     P  ON OI."product_id" = P."id"
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"       O  ON OI."order_id"  = O."order_id"
WHERE  O."created_at" BETWEEN 1564617600000000 /* 2019‑08‑01 */
                         AND 1567295999000000 /* 2019‑08‑31 23:59:59 */
GROUP  BY P."category"
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Get all June 2019 category aggregates that will serve as the growth baseline.
SELECT P."category",
       COUNT(*)                           AS "orders_jun",
       SUM(OI."sale_price")               AS "revenue_jun",
       SUM(OI."sale_price" - P."cost")    AS "profit_jun"
FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  OI
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"     P  ON OI."product_id" = P."id"
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"       O  ON OI."order_id"  = O."order_id"
WHERE  O."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 /* 2019‑06‑01 */
                         AND 1561939199000000 /* 2019‑06‑30 23:59:59 */
GROUP  BY P."category"
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Month‑by‑month aggregates (June‑Dec 2019) that will later feed MoM growth logic.
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(O."created_at"/1000000), 'YYYY-MM')  AS "yyyymm",
       P."category",
       COUNT(*)                                                  AS "num_order_items",
       SUM(OI."sale_price")                                      AS "revenue",
       SUM(OI."sale_price" - P."cost")                           AS "profit"
FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  OI
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"     P  ON OI."product_id" = P."id"
JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"       O  ON OI."order_id"  = O."order_id"
WHERE  O."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 /* 2019‑06‑01 */
                         AND 1577836799000000 /* 2019‑12‑31 */
GROUP  BY 1, P."category"
ORDER  BY 1, 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as #8 but restricting to July‑Dec and adding MoM % growth versus June baseline.
WITH monthly AS (
    SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(O."created_at"/1000000), 'YYYY-MM')  AS "yyyymm",
           P."category",
           COUNT(*)                           AS "orders_cnt",
           SUM(OI."sale_price")               AS "revenue",
           SUM(OI."sale_price" - P."cost")    AS "profit"
    FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  OI
    JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"     P  ON OI."product_id" = P."id"
    JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"       O  ON OI."order_id"  = O."order_id"
    WHERE  O."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 /* 2019‑06‑01 */
                             AND 1577836799000000 /* 2019‑12‑31 */
    GROUP  BY 1, P."category"
),
jun AS (
    SELECT "category",
           "orders_cnt"  AS "orders_jun",
           "revenue"     AS "revenue_jun",
           "profit"      AS "profit_jun"
    FROM   monthly
    WHERE  "yyyymm" = '2019-06'
)
SELECT m."yyyymm",
       m."category",
       m."orders_cnt",
       m."revenue",
       m."profit",
       100 * (m."orders_cnt" - j."orders_jun")  / NULLIF(j."orders_jun", 0)   AS "orders_mom_%_vs_jun",
       100 * (m."revenue"   - j."revenue_jun") / NULLIF(j."revenue_jun", 0)  AS "revenue_mom_%_vs_jun",
       100 * (m."profit"    - j."profit_jun")  / NULLIF(j."profit_jun", 0)   AS "profit_mom_%_vs_jun"
FROM   monthly  m
JOIN   jun       j  ON m."category" = j."category"
WHERE  m."yyyymm" <> '2019-06'
ORDER  BY m."yyyymm", m."category"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Preview final‑looking report for September 2019 only (orders, revenue, profit, MoM growth).
WITH jun AS (
    SELECT P."category",
           COUNT(*)                        AS "orders_jun",
           SUM(OI."sale_price")            AS "revenue_jun",
           SUM(OI."sale_price"-P."cost")   AS "profit_jun"
    FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" OI
    JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"    P  ON OI."product_id" = P."id"
    JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"      O  ON OI."order_id"  = O."order_id"
    WHERE  O."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1561939199000000
    GROUP  BY P."category"
),
sep AS (
    SELECT P."category",
           COUNT(*)                        AS "orders_sep",
           SUM(OI."sale_price")            AS "revenue_sep",
           SUM(OI."sale_price"-P."cost")   AS "profit_sep"
    FROM   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" OI
    JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"    P  ON OI."product_id" = P."id"
    JOIN   THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDERS"      O  ON OI."order_id"  = O."order_id"
    WHERE  O."created_at" BETWEEN 1567296000000000 /* 2019‑09‑01 */
                             AND 1569887999000000 /* 2019‑09‑30 */
    GROUP  BY P."category"
)
SELECT s."category",
       s."orders_sep",
       s."revenue_sep",
       s."profit_sep",
       100*(s."orders_sep" - j."orders_jun")  / NULLIF(j."orders_jun",0)  AS "orders_growth_vs_jun_%",
       100*(s."revenue_sep"- j."revenue_jun") / NULLIF(j."revenue_jun",0) AS "revenue_growth_vs_jun_%",
       100*(s."profit_sep" - j."profit_jun")  / NULLIF(j."profit_jun",0)  AS "profit_growth_vs_jun_%"
FROM   sep s
JOIN   jun j ON s."category" = j."category"
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progressively expose the tables, keys, date handling, aggregation logic, and finally the month‑over‑month (MoM) growth calculation methodology you can extend for the full July‑to‑December 2019 deliverable.
